+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""
+lerobot-record  --robot.type=koch_follower  --robot.port=COM3  --robot.id=my_awesome_follower_arm \
+    --robot.cameras="{ front: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 2, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}, wrist: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 3, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}}" \
+    --display_data=true --dataset.repo_id=a/b --dataset.root='d:/dataset/test' \
+    --dataset.single_task="pick the green toy and place into box" \
+    --policy.pretrained_path='C:/Users/admin/Desktop/smolvla' --policy.type=smolvla \
+    --policy.vlm_model_name='./smolvlm2_500m' --policy.device='cuda'
+
+
+VLA-adapted record script for Being-H05 Koch follower arm.
+
+This script extends LeRobot's ``lerobot_record.py`` to support autonomous
+VLA inference (Being-H05) instead of human teleoperation.
+
+Two operation modes:
+    1. **VLA mode** (--vla.model_path set): Uses Being-H05 VLA for autonomous
+       action generation. No teleoperator needed.
+    2. **Teleop mode** (--teleop.type set): Standard human teleoperation
+       recording. Same as original lerobot_record.py.
+
+
+=== VLA Mode Usage Examples ===
+
+Minimal (VLA-only, no recording):
+    python lerobot_record_vla.py \\
+        --robot.type=koch_follower \\
+        --robot.port=/dev/ttyUSB0 \\
+        --robot.cameras="{above: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 0, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}, wrist: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 1, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}}" \\
+        --vla.model_path=/path/to/Being-H05/checkpoints/step-10000 \\
+        --vla.single_task="pick up the orange block" \\
+        --control.fps=20 \\
+        --control.num_steps=200
+
+VLA + recording to LeRobot dataset:
+    python lerobot_record_vla.py \\
+        --robot.type=koch_follower \\
+        --robot.port=/dev/ttyUSB0 \\
+        --robot.cameras="{above: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 0, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}, wrist: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 1, width: 640, height: 480, fps: 30}}" \\
+        --vla.model_path=/path/to/Being-H05/checkpoints/step-10000 \\
+        --vla.single_task="pick up the orange block" \\
+        --vla.num_inference_timesteps=4 \\
+        --control.fps=20 \\
+        --dataset.repo_id=my_user/koch_vla_eval \\
+        --dataset.num_episodes=5 \\
+        --dataset.single_task="pick up the orange block" \\
+        --display_data=true
+
+VLA with custom camera keys:
+    python lerobot_record_vla.py \\
+        --robot.type=koch_follower \\
+        --robot.port=/dev/ttyUSB0 \\
+        --robot.cameras="{laptop: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 0, ...}, phone: {type: opencv, index_or_path: 1, ...}}" \\
+        --vla.model_path=/path/to/checkpoint \\
+        --vla.camera_above_key=laptop \\
+        --vla.camera_wrist_key=phone \\
+        --vla.single_task="pick up the orange block"
+
+
+=== Data Flow (VLA Mode) ===
+
+       [ Cameras: above + wrist ]
+       [ Motors: 6x Dynamixel  ]
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ robot.get_observation() ]
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ obs → Being-H05 format ]  ───  raw_obs_to_beingh_obs()
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ BeingHPolicy.get_action() ]  ───  Flow Matching ODE (4 steps)
+                │                                         │
+                │                              ViT encodes 2 images
+                │                              LLM + Action Expert predicts
+                │                              16-step action chunk
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ Being-H05 output → robot action ]
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ robot.send_action() ]  ───  Execute first action
+                │
+                ▼
+       [ Optionally record to LeRobot dataset ]
+"""
